PART C: HANDS-ON PRACTICE – CREATE JENKINS PIPELINE USING SCRIPT
Step 1: Open Jenkins
Open http://localhost:8080.

Click New Item.

Step 2: Create Pipeline Job
Enter project name: MavenJava_Pipeline.

Select Pipeline.

Click OK.

Step 3: General Configuration
Enter Description:
Maven Java Pipeline Automation.

Configure Build Triggers if required by the question.

Leave other settings as default.

Step 4: Configure Pipeline Script
Scroll down to Pipeline.

Definition: Select Pipeline script.

In the Script box, paste the following code.

Step 5: Jenkins Pipeline Script
Replace the GitHub URL with your actual Maven Java repository URL.

pipeline {
    agent any

    tools {
        maven 'MAVEN-HOME'
    }

    stages {

        stage('Git Repo & Clean') {
            steps {
                bat 'git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git mavenjava'
                bat 'mvn clean -f mavenjava'
            }
        }

        stage('Install') {
            steps {
                bat 'mvn install -f mavenjava'
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                bat 'mvn test -f mavenjava'
            }
        }

        stage('Package') {
            steps {
                bat 'mvn package -f mavenjava'
            }
        }
    }
}


